The eMMC on the AMD FCH SD/eMMC controller (PCI 1022:7906), as on the XGS 87.

Against FreeBSD 15.1's sys/dev/mmc and sys/dev/sdhci, the sources of the
OPNsense 26.7 kernel; applied with `patch -p1` from the directory that holds
sys/.  docs/findings/the-emmc-of-the-xgs-87-and-the-bus-test.md says what the
fault is, what each change is for and what has not been run yet.

mmc: a host capability, MMC_CAP_NO_BUS_TEST, for a host that cannot take the
  CMD19/CMD14 bus test.  On such a host the width is found the way Linux finds
  it on every host: the card is switched with CMD6, EXT_CSD is read again over
  the new width, and the width is kept only when its read-only fields read
  back as they did over the 1-bit bus; 1 bit otherwise.  And ERASE_GROUP_DEF
  is set before the width is looked for, on every host, as Linux does: while
  the bus is still the 1-bit one the card came up on.

sdhci: a quirk, SDHCI_QUIRK_CLEAR_TRANSFER_MODE, off unless a front end sets
  it: Transfer Mode written 0 before a command without data, as Linux's
  SDHCI_QUIRK2_CLEAR_TRANSFERMODE_REG_BEFORE_CMD.

sdhci_pci: an entry for 1022:7906 that sets the capability, and the quirk
  where the chipset's SMBus says it needs it (Linux's amd_probe()).

